    "created_at": "2019-10-01T18:21:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-01T18:21:52Z",
    "body": "I regret saying arbitrary, that seems to carry a heavier meaning than I intended.\r\n\r\nHTML is a great format for exchanging information in all sorts of fields, not limited to the world of computing, and as long as the parsing definition supports higher precision anyway (and so does the ISO this is loosely based on) I am not really convinced that computing (at least ECMAScript, IIRC) going for millisecond precision should limit what can be documented in HTML.",
